{
 "_comment": [
  "FRED series definitions. Each pillar has a directional AXIS; `polarity` states whether a",
  "rising value pushes that pillar UP its axis (+1) or DOWN (-1).",
  "  pillar 1 growth      axis up = EXPANDING",
  "  pillar 2 inflation   axis up = HOTTER",
  "  pillar 3 conditions  axis up = TIGHTER",
  "  pillar 4 credit      axis up = MORE STRESS / DRAINING",
  "  pillar 5 breadth     axis up = HEALTHIER",
  "  pillar 6 structural  descriptive only, not scored",
  "  pillar 7 debt chain  descriptive only, not scored - feeds the Debt & Debasement tracker",
  "`anchor` is a STRUCTURAL boundary (definitional, not a guessed level): ISM 50 by",
  "construction, Sahm 0.50 by definition, 0.0 for spreads that invert or indices centered",
  "on zero. Everything else is scored against its own trailing distribution.",
  "`transform`: level | diff | mom_pct | yoy_pct",
  "  pillar 8 ai credit   descriptive only, not scored - feeds the AI Credit tracker"
 ],
